":100},"card":{"id":"L25/N2002","status":"mixed","status_from":"run","run_status":"mixed","versions":[{"v":1,"kind":"automated","author":"deepseek/deepseek-v3.2","created":"2026-10-26T19:14:49Z","blind":true,"confidence":"medium","label":"emotional question mark and first-person emotional response","no_coherent_hypothesis":false,"trigger_hypothesis":"The neuron activates strongly on question marks ('?') that end emotionally charged questions, especially those expressing uncertainty, conflict, or seeking validation about personal/emotional situations. It also activates on first-person emotional responses (like 'I am') that follow emotional user statements.","output_hypothesis":"The neuron's output pushes toward tokens that indicate a continuation or elaboration, like ellipsis and newlines, suggesting it encourages the model to extend emotional or uncertain narratives with further detail or reflection.","alternatives":["The neuron detects sentence-final punctuation (question marks, periods) in emotional or conversational contexts.","The neuron responds to tokens that signal a transition to a new speaker or segment in dialogue, like newlines and commas."],"adapter_changes":"State B+1 strongly increases activation on newline tokens in chat contexts (W13, W15) and generally amplifies positive activations in chat domains. State A+1 amplifies positive activations across many contexts (W14, W16, W17). States C+1 and E+1 show more muted changes, with E+1 sometimes reducing activation in chat continuations.","supporting":["L25_N2002:e01","L25_N2002:e03","L25_N2002:e06","L25_N2002:e07","L25_N2002:e20"],"contradicting":["L25_N2002:e11","L25_N2002:e24","L25_N2002:e23","L25_N2002:e13","L25_N2002:e32","L25_N2002:e31","L25_N2002:e30","L25_N2002:e29"],"proposed_tests":["Emotional question mark vs. neutral question mark :: [high] Are you feeling crazy or am I crazy? | [low] What is the capital of France?","First-person emotional response vs. third-person statement :: [high] I am so s